      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the (undocumented) C code, I don\u0027t think it is safe to use the result of `fdt_next_node` when it returns a negative `depth` as `nextoffset` (its return value) then points to the next _tag_, not _node_. For the same reason, the function also seems to be broken for negative `depth` input values, so let\u0027s not count on those.\n\nIMO, this could be addressed by abstracting away the signedness of `depth` (the C `int*`) by taking a `usize` and returning `None` when the returned value is finally negative. I think it would make the API more \"Rusty\" and would probably be easier to wrap in an `Iterator`.",
